  linear-gradient(110deg, transparent 0 5%, #ef9500 5.5% 6%, transparent 6.5% 10%, #ef9500 10.5% 11%, transparent 11.5% 18%, #ef9500 18.5% 19%, transparent 19.5% 27%, #ef9500 27.5% 28%, transparent 28.5% 38%, #ef9500 38.5% 39%, transparent 39.5% 49%, #ef9500 49.5% 50%, transparent 50.5% 62%, #ef9500 62.5% 63%, transparent 63.5% 77%, #ef9500 77.5% 78%, transparent 78.5% 89%, #ef9500 89.5% 90%, transparent 90.5%);\n  }\n\n  .spectrogram-box {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 152px;\n    top: 164px;\n    width: 166px;\n    height: 50px;\n    border: 3px dashed #efeb72;\n    background: #fffff8;\n  }\n\n  .spectrogram-title {\n    margin-top: 1px;\n  }\n\n  .spectrum-line {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 10px;\n    right: 8px;\n    bottom: 8px;\n    height: 20px;\n    border-left: 1px solid #aaa;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #aaa;\n    background: linear-gradient(178deg, transparent 0 18%, #3159b0 20% 23%, transparent 25% 74%, #3159b0 76% 80%, transparent 82%);\n  }\n\n  .chart-area {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 34px;\n    top: 13px;\n    width: 243px;\n    height: 179px;\n    border: 1px solid #999;\n    background: #fff;\n  }\n\n  .chart-y-title {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: -32px;\n    top: 67px;\n    width: 105px;\n    transform: rotate(-90deg);\n    transform-origin: center;\n    font-size: 8px;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n\n  .chart-x-title {\n    position: absolute;\n    bottom: -21px;\n    left: 65px;\n    width: 130px;\n    font-size: 8px;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n\n  .frequency-bars {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 14px;\n    top: 18px;\n    width: 207px;\n    height: 146px;\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-rows: repeat(5, 19px);\n    row-gap: 10px;\n  }\n\n  .frequency-row {\n    position: relative;\n    height: 19px;\n    border-radius: 12px;\n    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #261090, #15017f 45%, #251192 100%);\n  }\n\n  .dot {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 1px;\n    width: 17px;\n    height: 17px;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    background: #7a0da3;\n  }\n\n  .dot.hot {\n    background: #ff7449;\n  }\n\n  .dot.mid {\n    background: #ca2877;\n  }\n\n  .colorbar {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 7px;\n    top: 13px;\n    width: 9px;\n    height: 178px;\n    border: 1px solid #aaa;\n    background: linear-gradient(to top, #160487, #8c0aa5, #ec4370, #ffe625);\n  }\n\n  .colorbar-title {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: -22px;\n    top: 71px;\n    width: 110px;\n    transform: rotate(-90deg);\n    transform-origin: center;\n    font-size: 8px;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n\n  .ticks {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 2px;\n    right: 2px;\n    bottom: -13px;\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    font-size: 7px;\n  }\n\n  .figure-caption {\n    margin: 0 0 25px 1px;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 21px;\n    line-height: 1.12;\n    text-align: left;\n  }\n\n  .right .result {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr;\n    margin: 0 0 40px 27px;\n    font-size: 27px;\n    line-height: 1.185;\n  }\n\n  .result-index {\n    font-style: italic;\n  }\n\n  .section-heading {\n    margin: 0 0 9px 0;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 27px;\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-weight: 400;\n  }\n\n  .setup-text {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr;\n    margin-left: 27px;\n  }\n\n  mjx-container {\n    margin: 0 !important;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"page\">\n  <header class=\"running-head\">IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON INDUSTRIAL ELECTRONICS</header>\n\n  <div class=\"columns\">\n    <section class=\"column left\">\n      <div class=\"numbered\">\n        <div class=\"index\">3)</div>\n        <div class=\"content\">\n          <p><span class=\"bold\">LSTM Update:</span> The input vector \\(\\mathbf{x}_m\\) and the previous hidden states \\((h_{m-1}, C_{m-1})\\) are fed into the LSTM cell to compute the updated states \\((h_m, C_m)\\):</p>\n          <div class=\"equation-row\">\n            <div class=\"equation\">\\((h_m, C_m)=\\mathrm{LSTM}(\\mathbf{x}_m,(h_{m-1},C_{m-1}))\\)</div>\n            <div class=\"equation-number\">(7)</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"numbered step-4\">\n        <div class=\"index\">4)</div>\n        <div class=\"content\">\n          <p><span class=\"bold\">Force Increment Prediction:</span> A Multi-Layer Perceptron, denoted as \\(\\mathrm{MLP}_{\\Delta f}\\), regresses the high-frequency normal force increment \\(\\Delta\\hat f_m\\) for the current time window derived from the hidden state \\(h_m\\):</p>\n          <div class=\"equation-row\">\n            <div class=\"equation\">\\(\\Delta\\hat f_m=\\mathrm{MLP}_{\\Delta f}(h_m)\\in\\mathbb{R}\\)</div>\n            <div class=\"equation-number\">(8)</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"numbered step-5\">\n        <div class=\"index\">5)</div>\n        <div class=\"content\">\n          <p><span class=\"bold\">Force Accumulation:</span> The current normal force estimate is updated sequentially. This intermediate prediction relies purely on the integration of the fast-adapting event stream:</p>\n          <div class=\"equation-row\">\n            <div class=\"equation\">\\(\\hat f_m=\\hat f_{m-1}+\\Delta\\hat f_m\\)</div>\n            <div class=\"equation-number\">(9)</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"after-equation\">After iterating through all \\(M\\) packets within the cycle, an accumulated normal force estimate \\(\\hat f_M\\), driven purely by the transient event stream, is obtained.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"subsection\"><span class=\"lead\">d) Fusion Feature Construction:</span> To counteract integration drift, we concatenate the final accumulated event driven force, \\(\\hat f_M\\), with the absolute spatial guide frame feature, \\(\\mathbf{f}_{\\mathrm{frame}}\\), constructing a unified multimodal fusion vector, \\(\\mathbf{f}_{\\mathrm{fusion}}\\):</p>\n      <div class=\"equation-row subsection-equation\">\n        <div class=\"equation\">\\(\\mathbf{f}_{\\mathrm{fusion}}=[\\hat f_M;\\mathbf{f}_{\\mathrm{frame}}]\\in\\mathbb{R}^{1+D_f}\\)</div>\n        <div class=\"equation-number\">(10)</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subsection\"><span class=\"lead\">e) Correction Term Prediction:</span> The fusion feature \\(\\mathbf{f}_{\\mathrm{fusion}}\\) is processed by calibration network \\((\\mathrm{MLP}_{\\mathrm{corr}})\\) to predict a 1D force correction term, \\(\\Delta f_{\\mathrm{corr}}\\). This component explicitly learns to compensate for accumulated drift by anchoring the estimate to the reliable absolute spatial deformation captured by the image frame:</p>\n      <div class=\"equation-row subsection-equation\">\n        <div class=\"equation\">\\(\\Delta f_{\\mathrm{corr}}=\\mathrm{MLP}_{\\mathrm{corr}}(\\mathbf{f}_{\\mathrm{fusion}})\\in\\mathbb{R}\\)</div>\n        <div class=\"equation-number\">(11)</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subsection\"><span class=\"lead\">f) Final Force Output:</span> The corrective term is seamlessly added to the accumulated force to yield the final, drift compensated normal force estimate for the current temporal cycle, \\(\\hat f_{\\mathrm{final}}\\):</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"column right\">\n      <p class=\"intro\">Following Funk et al. [11] , a resonant speaker (Adin S9WiFi) is placed in direct contact with the silicone surface to maximize vibration energy transfer (Fig. 3(a)). Sinusoidal audio stimuli ranging from 50 to 250 Hz are applied. To process the data, raw asynchronous events are binned into 2 ms windows, generating a 500 Hz synchronous event rate signal.</p>\n\n      <figure class=\"figure placeholder\" aria-label=\"Experimental setup and normalized frequency spectrum\">\n        <span class=\"placeholder-description\">[Diagram: centered experimental setup and normalized frequency spectrum]</span>\n\n        <div class=\"setup-panel\">\n          <span class=\"panel-label\">(a)</span>\n          <div class=\"speaker\">\n            <div class=\"speaker-top\"></div>\n            <div class=\"speaker-ring\"></div>\n            <div class=\"sensor-body\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"arrow-left\"></div>\n          <div class=\"speaker-note\">Speaker plays a 100Hz sine wave</div>\n          <div class=\"vibration-arrow\"></div>\n          <div class=\"vibration-label\">Vibration</div>\n          <div class=\"signal-arrow\"></div>\n          <div class=\"event-box\">\n            <div class=\"event-title\">Event Rate Plot</div>\n            <div class=\"event-plot\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"spectrogram-box\">\n            <div class=\"spectrogram-title\">Spectrogram</div>\n            <div class=\"spectrum-line\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"chart-panel\">\n          <span class=\"panel-label\">(b)</span>\n          <div class=\"chart-area\">\n            <div class=\"chart-y-title\">Input Signal Frequency \\(f_s\\) (Hz)</div>\n            <div class=\"frequency-bars\">\n              <div class=\"frequency-row\">\n                <span class=\"dot\" style=\"left:39px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot\" style=\"left:60px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot\" style=\"left:105px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot\" style=\"left:169px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot\" style=\"left:190px\"></span>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"frequency-row\">\n                <span class=\"dot hot\" style=\"left:148px\"></span>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"frequency-row\">\n                <span class=\"dot\" style=\"left:43px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot hot\" style=\"left:105px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot\" style=\"left:169px\"></span>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"frequency-row\">\n                <span class=\"dot\" style=\"left:20px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot mid\" style=\"left:62px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot mid\" style=\"left:148px\"></span>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"frequency-row\">\n                <span class=\"dot hot\" style=\"left:19px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot mid\" style=\"left:62px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot mid\" style=\"left:105px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot mid\" style=\"left:148px\"></span>\n                <span class=\"dot\" style=\"left:190px\"></span>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"ticks\">\n              <span>0</span><span>50</span><span>100</span><span>150</span><span>200</span><span>250</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"chart-x-title\">Frequency (Hz)</div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"colorbar\"></div>\n          <div class=\"colorbar-title\">Normalized Amplitude</div>\n        </div>\n      </figure>\n\n      <figcaption class=\"figure-caption\">Fig. 3. Experimental setup and results for high-frequency vibration sensing. (a) A resonant Bluetooth speaker (Adin S9WiFi) is placed directly on the Mixtac sensor to act as a vibration source. (b) Normalized frequency spectrum obtained from Mixtac’s raw event stream under various input tones. The spectrum was generated by applying a Fourier transform to the event count time series. The resulting prominent diagonal pattern indicates a strong linear correlation, confirming that the reconstructed frequency consistently matches the speaker’s input frequency up to the tested maximum of 250 Hz.</figcaption>\n\n      <div class=\"result\">\n        <div class=\"result-index\">2)</div>\n        <p><span class=\"italic\">Result:</span> The results confirm that Mixtac can reconstruct high frequency vibrations from its raw event stream. The reconstructed dominant frequency remains in close agreement with the speaker input frequency over 50 to 250 Hz in (Fig. 3(b)). This range is close to the Nyquist limit of the 500 Hz acquisition rate.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <h2 class=\"section-heading\">B. Stability of Long Term Force Estimation</h2>\n\n      <div class=\"setup-text\">\n        <div class=\"result-index\">1)</div>\n        <p><span class=\"italic\">Experimental Setup:</span> This experiment examines whether the model remains stable during sustained contact. To reveal long term drift, the sensor was pressed for about 25 s with an 18 mm hemispherical 3D printed indenter while mounted on a 6 axis force sensor operating at 800 Hz. Stability was quantified by the MAE between the predicted and ground truth</p>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>"
